{
  "version": 2,
  "_comment": "Shipped firewall policy (v2). AUTHORITATIVE runtime copy: packages/core/policies/default.json is a byte-identical mirror (verify.mjs enforces it). Override with PI_KIT_FIREWALL_POLICY=/path/to/policy.json. Shell commands are analysed by tool-firewall's parser and classifier (tiers low/medium/high/critical), not by regexes; `tools` pins non-shell tools (allow = known, content still analysed; ask = always ask a human; deny = never). `defaults.unknown` applies to tools with no entry and no read-only name. `command_rules` are OPERATOR rules matched in every policy against the raw command and each parsed step (deny -> critical, ask -> high). `policies.pentest.command_rules` add the strict engagement rules (a superset of pentest-governance-domain's DESTRUCTIVE_COMMANDS, checked by verify.mjs) when firewall.json selects the pentest policy.",
